{
  "title": "Dua-e-Hifz-e-Eemaan رَضِيْتُ بِاللّٰهِ رَبًّا",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "It is also worth mentioning that Shaykh al-Tusi has narrated that Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Daylami said to Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) “Your adherents say that Faith is of two sections; one is steady and the other depository. So, please teach me a supplication that makes my faith perfect and saves it from removal.” Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) hence taught him to say the following supplicatory prayer after each obligatory prayer:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nرَضِيْتُ بِاللّٰهِ رَبًّا\nRAZEETO BILLAAHE RABBANW\nI am content with Allah as my Lord, \nوَّ بِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهِ نَبِيًّا\nWA BE-MOHAMMADIN SALLAL LAAHO A'LAYHE WA AALEHI NABIYYAN \nand with Muhammad (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his progeny) as a Prophet, \nوَ بِالْاِسْلَامِ دِيْنًا\nWA BIL-ISLAAME DEENAN\nand with Islam as a religion, \nوَ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ كِتَابًا\nWA BIL-QUR-AANE KETAABAN\nand with the Qur'an as a book, \nوَ بِالْكَعْبَةِ قِبْلَةً\nWA BIL-KA'BATE QIBLATAN \nand with the Ka'bah as the direction (of prayer - Qiblah), \nوَ بِعَلِيٍّ وَلِيًّا وَّ اِمَامًا\nWA BE-A'LIYYIN WALIYYANW WA EMAAMAN\nand with Ali as a Guardian (Wali) and Imam, \nوَ بِالْحَسَنِ وَ الْحُسَيْنِ\nWA BIL-HASANE WAL HUSAYNE\nand with al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, \nوَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ\nWA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYNE\nAli ibn al-Husain, \nوَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nWA MOHAMMAD IBNE A'LIYYIN\nand Muhammad ibn Ali, \nوَ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA JA'FAR IBNE MOHAMMADIN\nand Ja’far ibn Muhammad, \nوَ مُوْسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ\nWA MOOSABNE JA'FARIN\nand Moosa ibn Ja’far,\nوَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى\nWA A'LIYY IBNE MOOSAA\nand Ali ibn Moosa, \nوَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nWA MOHAMMAD IBNE A'LIYYIN\nand Muhammad ibn Ali, \nوَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA A'LIYY IBNE MOHAMMADIN\nand Ali ibn Muhammad,\nوَ الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ\nWAL HASAN IBNE A'LIYYIN\nand al-Hasan ibn Ali, \nوَ الْحُجَّةِ بْنِ الْحَسَنِ\nWAL HUJJAT IBNIL HASANE\nand the Proof [of Allah] the son of al-Hasan,\nصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِمْ اَئِمَّةً\nSALAWAATUL LAAHE A'LAYHIM A-IMMATAN\nmay the blessings of Allah be upon them, as Imams (Leaders)\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ رَضِيْتُ بِهِمْ اَئِمَّةً\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE RAZEETO BEHIM A-IMMATAN\nO Allah, indeed I am content with them as Imams, \nفَارْضَنِيْ لَهُمْ\nFARZANEE LAHUM\nso make me content with them.\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ.\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nSurely, You have power over all things."
}
